## 5. COLLISIONS THE CHANGE FORCES (pinned by reading, all three named)

1. **`row_class()` shape inference goes unsound at W=128** — a narrow
   padded plan (rows=128) would classify Wide. FIXED by HUNK B: the
   plan carries its own arm; the class is a fact, never inferred. (A
   type-law improvement independent of the budget ask: today's
   inference is sound only because 4 < 128.)
2. **The dense dispatch would take wide m=128** (tiles=1, total==m) —
   the shared-staging form defect 3 condemned. FIXED by HUNK C.
3. **HELD FOR YOUR RULING — the cross-class plan-disagreement guard
   goes blind.** At W=128 the wide tile and the narrow padded part are
   BOTH [128, k] footprints, so the byte-compare guard
   (ktir_matmul_fp8.rs:1096-1108, and the narrow arm's twin) can no
   longer distinguish them: `a_second_gemm_at_a_different_row_class_
   refuses` loses its trigger — the second GEMM at n=64 over the same
   activation would be silently ACCEPTED as reuse where today it
   refuses. The typed stagings (`Fp8TileStaging<128>` vs
   `Fp8NarrowStaging`) also converge on 128 rows, so the row-count
   refusal inside `staged()` cannot distinguish them either.

   My recommended shape, fail-closed: the synth reservation carries
   the arm — a `wide` tag recorded beside `sizes` at reservation time,
   and the footprint guard refuses on `have_wide != want_wide` as well
   as on bytes. The test then passes VERBATIM (the refusal still
   fires, now on the arm). The alternative — prove the converged reuse
   correct and flip the test to a reuse pin — I do NOT recommend: the
   two staging types exist precisely because nobody proved the walks
   agree, and an unproven convergence is the defect-3 class again. If
   you rule the tag shape, I bring its exact diff (BundleLayout
   surface + both guards) as a rider to this proposal before anything
   lands.

## Behavior delta

The wide arm's row tile: 4 → 128. Every wide multi-tile geometry's
emission changes (fewer, taller tiles — the rung bodies 256/512 go
from 64/128 tiles to 2/4). Numerics unchanged by construction
(per-token scales, row-independent mm, row splice). Decode (m=1)
byte-identical. Narrow arm unchanged. Dense arm unchanged except the
m=128-wide guard. The 256 rung, 512 rung, window, and all three budget
walls hold — see §3. Nothing here lands without your ruling; the rider
batch rides the same rsync.
